uninstalled + hook-bypassing; CI `secret-pattern-policy` was `main`-only; the leak was on `logan/obsidian`), and the guard matched **paths/tokens not secret material** (POSIWID — Logan's correction). Rewrote `.github/scripts/check_secret_patterns.py` to detect content path-independently (DER private keys armored+unarmored PKCS#1/PKCS#8/EC/Ed, base64 auth blobs, high-entropy raw key blobs); proven a renamed hostkey + innocently-named unarmored key are caught; false-positive load 43→3. Broadened CI to all branches; narrowed path rules + gitignore to a credential-filename belt. `git filter-repo` purged the 4 secret paths from all history (4,049 commits), force-pushed; **verified 0 carrying commits across all 163 branches**, `main` never affected, remote scrubbed (API-confirmed). Full record: [`SECRET-LEAK-INCIDENT-2026-07-02.md`](SECRET-LEAK-INCIDENT-2026-07-02.md). **RESOLVED 2026-07-02 — ADB + Dropbox keys rotated by Logan; the exposed material is now dead. Residual (inert with keys rotated): GitHub retains `0ae47c135` by SHA until GC (Support can expedite); forks retain old history.** Doctrinal corrections absorbed: dotdirs ARE personae (don't exclude them); a secret guard must guard secret material (POSIWID); committer signature ≠ autonomous agent (the persona executed Logan's sort).\n32\t\n33\t- **Hermes op:// rollout.** Migrated 17 secret-bearing env vars in `~/.hermes/.env` from plaintext to 1Password references using the existing `OP_SERVICE_ACCOUNT_TOKEN`. Launcher shim invoked Hermes via `op run --env-file=~/.hermes/.env`. Filed `HERMES-WITNESS-COMPANION-2026-06-24.md`. *(Reverted 2026-06-30 — see Workaround revert below.)*\n34\t- **Fallback chain build.** Built an 18-entry `fallback_providers:` list in `~/.hermes/config.yaml` across OpenRouter, mistral-direct, anthropic-direct, perplexity-direct, opencode-zen, opencode-go, and ollama. Primary set to `mistralai/mistral-small-2603`. `provider_routing:` block set to `sort: price`, `data_collection: deny`. Custom provider entry added for perplexity-direct. `security.redact_secrets: true`.\n35\t- **Ollama hygiene.** Removed four unused models from the local store, recovering ~84 GB on a disk that was 95% full.\n36\t- **Env-loader override workaround.** Diagnosed `hermes_cli/env_loader.py:168` calling `_load_dotenv_with_fallback(user_env, override=True)`, which clobbered op-resolved env vars back to literal `op://...` strings on every chat subprocess spawn — root cause of Discord 401s across all cloud-routed calls. Split secrets out of `~/.hermes/.env` into a sibling `~/.hermes/.env.op` that `load_hermes_dotenv` does not read; rewrote the launcher shim to iterate `.env.op` and call `op read` per ref, exporting resolved values into process env before exec'ing the daemon. Documented in `~/.hermes/README-workaround.md` and `HERMES-WORKAROUND-WITNESS-2026-06-28.md`. *(Reverted 2026-06-30 — accumulating fragility relative to Hermes' upgrade machinery; see Workaround revert below.)*\n37\t- **Upstream cross-link.** Posted comments on `NousResearch/hermes-agent#19201` (cross-link), `#36949` (main cross-link with workaround case), and `#18734` (PR support with use case). Tracker breadcrumb left at `LAF-US/IDAHO-VAULT#690`. Filed first-external-contact witness `!/SIGNALS/TOUCHING-ME-TOUCHING-NOUS-2026-06-25.md` per Logan's \"Sweet Caroline pun\" naming.\n38\t- **BEEFSTACK switch design.** Mermaid VSM-style flowchart drafted with Logan (Router Core → Capability Analyzer → Tier → Provider → Locality → Cost → Hygiene → Endpoint). Implementation work paused pending Logan's open-decision answers (implementation surface, retry budget, cost meaning, capability-signal source, T1 tie-break).\n39\t- **Hidden-cache archived to vault per Logan's \"put it in the Vault\" directive.** Audited the 16 typed-memory files in `~/.claude/projects/-Users-logan/memory/`; salvaged 10 durable operational rules into the \"Operational Rules Salvaged…\" section of this anchor (each tagged with original cache fil