st attempt; secret-redaction config preserved; no 401 errors anywhere. The 1Password vault items remain the canonical source — `.env` is now derived plaintext, rotatable by re-running the same `op read` loop. 1Password integration to be re-attempted when Nous ships native support via `NousResearch/hermes-agent#36949`.\n41\t- **Tailscale Serve enabled for OpenClaw** (2026-07-01, ~01:09 PT). *(Superseded 2026-07-01 post-reboot — the Serve config never actually persisted; the gateway's `serve enabled` log line reports intent, not outcome. See \"Tailnet bind pivot\" below.)* `gateway.tailscale.mode: \"off\" → \"serve\"` via `openclaw config patch --stdin`; `gateway.bind: \"loopback\"` and `gateway.auth.mode: \"token\"` unchanged; bonjour workaround (`discovery.mdns.mode: \"off\"`) preserved. Daemon bounced clean. Post-change `openclaw status`: `Tailscale exposure: serve · logans-macbook-pro-1.tail7453f8.ts.net · https://logans-macbook-pro-1.tail7453f8.ts.net`. Pixel (100.68.197.104) can now reach the Mac's OpenClaw Gateway via that MagicDNS URL with TLS terminated by Tailscale Serve. Auth token stays at `~/.openclaw/openclaw.json` `gateway.auth.token`; retrieval via `python3 -c \"...\"|pbcopy` for clipboard paste into any client, never displayed in chat or committed. Pre-change config preserved at `~/openclaw-preupdate-backups/openclaw.json.pre-tailscale-serve.20260701-010906`. The VisionClaw witness's prerequisite chain was amended in place (step 1 marked complete with concrete URL) so the next Pixel rebuild has the deploy values on hand.\n42\t- **VisionClaw investigation companion filed** (2026-07-01). Four-layer stack mapped (Meta DAT SDK → CameraAccess samples → Sean Liu / Intent-Lab Gemini Live + OpenClaw wiring → Logan's LAF-US fork). Fork upstream corrected to [Intent-Lab/VisionClaw](https://github.com/Intent-Lab/VisionClaw) (not the `nichochar/openclaw` URL that appears twice in VisionClaw's own README — an upstream documentation-freshness artifact). Local check