{"parentUuid":"5bb9badc-ddb2-43f7-b3d6-aee6e3325924","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_011CcmhiVr1hiaFuiEtBHAdT","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This is the foundation, and it reframes today's 402 precisely. Two grounded findings already:\n\n1. **BEEFSTACK's whole thesis is \"diversify fallback by provider *bucket*, not model name\"** — and it explicitly warns that an OpenRouter **account-level** failure (credits/workspace) blows through *every* `openrouter/*` route at once. Today's 402 is exactly that: an account-credit failure. So even a model-diverse OpenRouter fallback chain wouldn't have saved it — only a *different bucket* (local Ollama, or a direct-provider BYOK key) escapes it.\n2. **The live OpenClaw config has drifted off BEEFSTACK.** BEEFSTACK specifies OpenClaw = local `devstral` primary + a 4-entry fallback chain; the gateway is running `mistral-medium-3-5` primary with `fallbackConfigured: false`. No belt, no suspenders.\n\nContinuing to read widely — the two snapshots, the OpenRouter key/account topology (bears on your two-provider setup + whether a second account has balance), and the #690 tracker:"}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":5886,"cache_creation_input_tokens":10752,"cache_read_input_tokens":277391,"output_tokens":4477,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":10752,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":5886,"output_tokens":4477,"cache_read_input_tokens":277391,"cache_creation_input_tokens":10752,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":10752},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CcmhiSpT7a6xyYWWu7wBk","type":"assistant","uuid":"cb970aee-94b1-4ea1-8d55-75af963cca15","timestamp":"2026-07-06T23