r correctly, but the OpenRouter route is rejected by backend budget/routing state.\n115\t\n116\t### Raw OpenRouter\n117\t\n118\tRaw calls were sent directly to:\n119\t\n120\t```text\n121\thttps://openrouter.ai/api/v1/chat/completions\n122\t```\n123\t\n124\tMistral test:\n125\t\n126\t```json\n127\t{\"model\":\"mistralai/mistral-small-2603\",\"messages\":[{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":\"Reply with exactly: RAW_OPENROUTER_OK\"}],\"max_tokens\":16}\n128\t```\n129\t\n130\tClaude test:\n131\t\n132\t```json\n133\t{\"model\":\"anthropic/claude-haiku-4.5\",\"messages\":[{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":\"Reply with exactly: RAW_CLAUDE_HAIKU_OK\"}],\"max_tokens\":16}\n134\t```\n135\t\n136\tBoth returned:\n137\t\n138\t```json\n139\t{\"error\":{\"message\":\"Budget limit exceeded (daily limit). Contact your org admin.\",\"code\":403}}\n140\t```\n141\t\n142\tConclusion: the 403 is not Hermes-specific.\n143\t\n144\t### OpenRouter Key Metadata\n145\t\n146\tOpenRouter key endpoint:\n147\t\n148\t```text\n149\tGET https://openrouter.ai/api/v1/key\n150\t```\n151\t\n152\tReported:\n153\t\n154\t```json\n155\t{\n156\t  \"limit\": null,\n157\t  \"limit_remaining\": null,\n158\t  \"include_byok_in_limit\": false,\n159\t  \"is_free_tier\": false,\n160\t  \"usage_daily\": 1.062516,\n161\t  \"byok_usage_daily\": 0.028164\n162\t}\n163\t```\n164\t\n165\tConclusion: this API key is not itself capped at the key level.\n166\t\n167\t### OpenCode\n168\t\n169\t`opencode providers list` reports credentials for:\n170\t\n171\t- OpenRouter\n172\t- Mistral\n173\t- Hugging Face\n174\t- GitHub Copilot\n175\t\n176\tInitial `opencode` calls inside sandbox hit a local SQLite checkpoint error. Retesting with normal filesystem permissions reached:\n177\t\n178\t```text\n179\tbuild - mistral-medium-latest\n180\t```\n181\t\n182\tbut did not return promptly and was stopped.\n183\t\n184\tConclusion: OpenCode has promising separate credential surfaces, but it was not yet validated as a clean Hermes fallback path in this pass.\n185\t\n186\t## OpenRouter Backend Investigation Targets\n187\t\n188\tLogan is investigating OpenRouter backend state. Highest-value checks:\n189\t\n190\t1. OpenRouter Activity page for the failed requests.\n191\t   - Open the failed generation.\n192\t   - Inspect raw metadata.\n193\t   - Look for `provider_responses`.\n194\t   - Confirm which provider endpoint returned the budget limit.\n195\t\n196\t2. OpenRouter BYOK settings.\n197\t   - Check Mistral provider key.\n198\t   - Check Anthropic provider key.\n199\t   - Look for daily/provider/org budget caps.\n200\t   - Check whether \"Always use for this provider\" is enabled.\n201\t\n202\t3. Workspace / org settings.\n203\t   - Check any daily budget cap at workspace/org level.\n204\t   - Check whether the user/API key is assigned to a project with a daily limit.\n205\t\n206\t4. Routing fallback behavior.\n207\t   - OpenRouter BYOK docs say prioritized BYOK keys are tried before shared OpenRouter endpoints.\n208\t   - \"Always use for this provider\" can prevent fallback to shared OpenRouter capacity.\n209\t   - BYOK provider ordering can override expected provider/model order.\n210\t\n211\tRelevant OpenRouter docs:\n212\t\n213\t- <https://openrouter.ai/docs/guides/overview/auth/byok>\n214\t- <https://openrouter.ai/docs/guides/routing/provider-selection>\n215\t- <https://openrouter.ai/docs/api/reference/limits>\n216\t\n217\t## Current Working Hypothesis\n218\t\n219\tThe OpenRouter API key is valid and uncapped, but requests are being routed into a provider/BYOK/workspace budget wall. The phrase \"Contact your org admin\" strongly suggests an org/workspace/provider-account budget constraint rather than a normal OpenRouter credit exhaustion condition.\n220\t\n221\tLikely fixes are in the OpenRouter dashboard, not in Hermes:\n222\t\n223\t- Adjust or remove a BYOK/provider daily budget.\n224\t- Disable \"Always use for this provider\" if shared OpenRouter capacity should be allowed.\n225\t- Move the affected BY