{"parentUuid":"8784f763-2e10-4e44-abde-19149d4abda1","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"3d256b37-5480-4f71-bca7-0e997cae6c19","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01L6LRneUjbiw835N5gBPmt6","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\ttitle: \"OpenRouter Management Key — Hermes Usage Guide\"\n3\tdate: 2026-05-23\n4\tstatus: live\n5\tauthority: LOGAN\n6\tdoc_class: reference\n7\trelated:\n8\t  - Hermes\n9\t  - OpenRouter\n10\t  - BEEFSTACK\n11\t  - \"PLAN-MANAGEMENT-KEY-TO-HERMES-2026-05-23\"\n12\t---\n13\t\n14\t## Where the key lives\n15\t\n16\tThe Management Key is set as `OPENROUTER_MANAGEMENT_KEY` in\n17\t`~/.hermes/.env` on the Mac. Hermes loads this at startup.\n18\t\n19\tThe canonical source of truth for the key value is 1Password on Windows\n20\t(LOGAN-ZBFURY), item `OpenRouter Management Key` in the `Private` vault,\n21\treadable via `op read \"op://Private/OpenRouter Management Key/credential\"`.\n22\t\n23\t## How Hermes calls the management API\n24\t\n25\tAll endpoints at `https://openrouter.ai/api/v1/keys`:\n26\t\n27\t### List all keys\n28\t```\n29\tterminal: curl -s -H \"Authorization: Bearer $OPENROUTER_MANAGEMENT_KEY\" https://openrouter.ai/api/v1/keys\n30\t```\n31\t\n32\t### Inspect a specific key (by hash)\n33\t```\n34\tterminal: curl -s -H \"Authorization: Bearer $OPENROUTER_MANAGEMENT_KEY\" https://openrouter.ai/api/v1/keys/<hash>\n35\t```\n36\t\n37\t### Create a new runtime key\n38\t```\n39\tterminal: curl -s -X POST -H \"Authorization: Bearer $OPENROUTER_MANAGEMENT_KEY\" -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" -d '{\"name\":\"agent-label\",\"limit\":100,\"limit_reset\":\"daily\"}' https://openrouter.ai/api/v1/keys\n40\t```\n41\t\n42\t### Disable a key\n43\t```\n44\tterminal: curl -s -X PATCH -H \"Authorization: Bearer $OPENROUTER_MANAGEMENT_KEY\" -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" -d '{\"disabled\":true}' https://openrouter.ai/api/v1/keys/<hash>\n45\t```\n46\t\n47\t### Update a key limit\n48\t```\n49\tterminal: curl -s -X PATCH -H \"Authorization: Bearer $OPENROUTER_MANAGEMENT_KEY\" -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" -d '{\"limit\":50,\"limit_reset\":\"daily\"}' https://openrouter.ai/api/v1/keys/<hash>\n50\t```\n51\t\n52\t### Delete a key\n53\t```\n54\tterminal: curl -s -X DELETE -H \"Authorization: Bearer $OPENROUTER_MANAGEMENT_KEY\" https://openrouter.ai/api/v1/keys/<hash>\n55\t```\n56\t\n57\t## Safety rules\n58\t\n59\t| Action | Autonomy | Notes |\n60\t|---|---|---|\n61\t| List keys, inspect metadata, check usage | Autonomous | Read-only, no Logan approval needed |\n62\t| Create runtime key with strict cap | Semi-autonomous | Inform Logan after creation |\n63\t| Disable a key | Semi-autonomous | Inform Logan after disabling |\n64\t| Delete a key | Requires Logan approval | Before execution |\n65\t| Raise a limit | Requires Logan approval | Before execution |\n66\t| Modify shared/production keys | Requires Logan approval | Before execution |\n67\t\n68\t## Audit requirement\n69\t\n70\tFor any mutation (create, disable, delete, limit change), write an audit\n71\tentry with: timestamp, actor, action, key hash prefix, old value, new\n72\tvalue, reason, approval source. Do not include full secret values.\n73\t\n74\t## Key context\n75\t\n76\t- The Management Key is a control-plane root for runtime keys only.\n77\t- It cannot be used for inference (`/api/v1/chat/completions`).\n78\t- It operates at the account level and can manage keys across workspaces.\n79\t- Never print the raw key value in transcripts, vault files, or logs.\n80\t\n81\t## Related docs\n82\t\n83\t- `!/PLAN-MANAGEMENT-KEY-TO-HERMES-2026-05-23.md` — transfer plan\n84\t- `!/OPENROUTER-RUNTIME-KEY-INVENTORY-WINDOWS-CODEX-2026-05-20.md` — Phase 1 inventory\n85\t- `!/BEEFSTACK-MODEL-ROUTING-2026-05-17.md` — BEEFSTACK architecture\n86\t"}]},"uuid":"1345dd3d-9c94-4ef5-beef-adbd30172c65","timestamp":"2026-07-07T00:01:39.487Z","toolUseResult":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/logan/IDAHO-VAULT/OPENROUTER-MANAGEMENT-KEY-USAGE-GUIDE-2026-05-23.md","content":"---\ntitle: \"OpenRouter Management Key — Hermes Usage Guide\"\ndate: 2026-05-23\nstatus: live\nauthority: LOGAN\ndoc_class: reference\nrelated:\n  - Hermes\n  - OpenRouter\n  - BEEFSTACK\n  - \"PLAN-MANAGEMENT-KEY-TO-HERMES-2026-05-23\"\n---\n\n## Where the key lives\n\nThe Management Key is set as `OPENROUTER_MANAGEMENT_KEY` in\n`~/.hermes/.env` on the Mac. Hermes loads this at startup.\n\nThe canonical source of truth for the key value is 1Password on Windows\n(LOGAN-ZBFURY), item `OpenRouter Management Key` in the `Private` vault,\nreadable via `op read \"op://Private/OpenRouter Management Key/credential\"`.\n\n## How Hermes calls the management API\n\nAll endpoints at `https://openrouter.ai/api/v1/keys`:\n\n### List all keys\n```\nterminal: curl -s -H \"Authorization: Bearer $OPENROUTER_MANAGEMENT_KEY\" https://openrouter.ai/api/v1/keys\n```\n\n### Inspect a specific key (by hash)\n```\nterminal: curl -s -H \"Authorization: Bearer $OPENROUTER_MANAGEMENT_KEY\" https://openrouter.ai/api/v1/keys/<hash>\n```\n\n### Create a new runtime key\n```\nterminal: curl -s -X POST -H \"Authorization: Bearer $OPENROUTER_MANAGEMENT_KEY\" -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" -d '{\"name\":\"agent-label\",\"limit\":100,\"limit_reset\":\"daily\"}' https://openrouter.ai/api/v1/keys\n```\n\n### Disable a key\n```\nterminal: curl -s -X PATCH -H \"Authorization: Bearer $OPENROUTER_MANAGEMENT_KEY\" -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" -d '{\"disabled\":true}' https://openrouter.ai/api/v1/keys/<hash>\n```\n\n### Update a key limit\n```\nterminal: curl -s -X PATCH -H \"Authorization: Bearer $OPENROUTER_MANAGEMENT_KEY\" -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" -d '{\"limit\":50,\"limit_reset\":\"daily\"}' https://openrouter.ai/api/v1/keys/<hash>\n```\n\n### Delete a key\n```\nterminal: curl -s -X DELETE -H \"Authorization: Bearer $OPENROUTER_MANAGEMENT_KEY\" https://openrouter.ai/api/v1/keys/<hash>\n```\n\n## Safety rules\n\n| Action | Autonomy | Notes |\n|---|---|---|\n| List keys, inspect metadata, check usage | Autonomous | Read-only, no Logan approval needed |\n| Create runtime key with strict cap | Semi-autonomous | Inform Logan after creation |\n| Disable a key | Semi-autonomous | Inform Logan after disabling |\n| Delete a key | Requires Logan approval | Before execution |\n| Raise a limit | Requires Logan approval | Before execution |\n| Modify shared/production keys | Requires Logan approval | Before execution |\n\n## Audit requirement\n\nFor any mutation (create, disable, delete, limit change), write an audit\nentry with: timestamp, actor, action, key hash prefix, old value, new\nvalue, reason, approval source. Do not include full secret values.\n\n## Key context\n\n- The Management Key is a control-plane root for runtime keys only.\n- It cannot be used for inference (`/api/v1/chat/completions`).\n- It operates at the account level and can manage keys across workspaces.\n- Never print the raw key value in transcripts, vault files, or logs.\n\n## Related docs\n\n- `!/PLAN-MANAGEMENT-KEY-TO-HERMES-2026-05-23.md` — transfer plan\n- `!/OPENROUTER-RUNTIME-KEY-INVENTORY-WINDOWS-CODEX-2026-05-20.md` — Phase 1 inventory\n- `!/BEEFSTACK-MODEL-ROUTING-2026-05-17.md` — BEEFSTACK architecture\n","numLines":86,"startLine":1,"totalLines":86}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"8784f763-2e10-4e44-abde-19149d4abda1","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/logan","sessionId":"4f03d270-3e64-41cc-b325-30871ab76d55","version":"2.1.202","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"your-18-entry-list-is-cached-gadget"}
