{"parentUuid":"6624ba5a-25fc-4f69-b62d-f8b73e54b312","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"744576ae-f99f-4592-a891-83f6e48038f1","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01PKLhXUB5vFRfNtotpbi7nx","type":"tool_result","content":"# Secrets Provider Configuration\n\n## Defining secrets.providers Entries\n\nProviders are configured under the `secrets.providers` object. Each provider requires a `source` type (\"env\", \"file\", or \"exec\") and a `provider` name matching the pattern `^[a-z][a-z0-9_-]{0,63}$`.\n\n## Exec Provider Fields\n\nFor an exec provider (e.g., vault):\n\n```json5\n{\n  source: \"exec\",\n  command: \"/usr/local/bin/openclaw-vault-resolver\",\n  args: [\"--profile\", \"prod\"],\n  passEnv: [\"PATH\", \"VAULT_ADDR\"],\n  jsonOnly: true,\n  allowSymlinkCommand: true,        // optional\n  trustedDirs: [\"/opt/homebrew\"],   // optional\n  timeoutMs: 5000,                   // optional\n  maxOutputBytes: 1048576            // optional\n}\n```\n\n## 1Password/op Provider Configuration\n\nThe documented example shows:\n\n```json5\n{\n  source: \"exec\",\n  command: \"/opt/homebrew/bin/op\",\n  allowSymlinkCommand: true,\n  trustedDirs: [\"/opt/homebrew\"],\n  args: [\"read\", \"op://Personal/OpenClaw QA API Key/password\"],\n  passEnv: [\"HOME\"],\n  jsonOnly: false\n}\n```\n\n## Binding to Model Providers\n\nA model provider's apiKey references a secret using the SecretRef object contract:\n\n```json5\n{\n  source: \"exec\",\n  provider: \"onepassword_openai\",\n  id: \"value\"\n}\n```\n\nThe `provider` field names the configured secrets provider; the `id` specifies what to retrieve from it.\n\n## Steps to Add a New Provider Secret\n\n1. \"Audit current state\" with `openclaw secrets audit --check`\n2. \"Configure and apply SecretRefs\" using `openclaw secrets configure --apply`\n3. \"Re-audit\" to verify the migration is complete"}]},"uuid":"ea8b1688-54b3-4017-9df4-e23f20491fc3","timestamp":"2026-07-07T04:37:36.067Z","toolUseResult":{"bytes":28683,"code":200,"codeText":"OK","result":"# Secrets Provider Configuration\n\n## Defining secrets.providers Entries\n\nProviders are configured under the `secrets.providers` object. Each provider requires a `source` type (\"env\", \"file\", or \"exec\") and a `provider` name matching the pattern `^[a-z][a-z0-9_-]{0,63}$`.\n\n## Exec Provider Fields\n\nFor an exec provider (e.g., vault):\n\n```json5\n{\n  source: \"exec\",\n  command: \"/usr/local/bin/openclaw-vault-resolver\",\n  args: [\"--profile\", \"prod\"],\n  passEnv: [\"PATH\", \"VAULT_ADDR\"],\n  jsonOnly: true,\n  allowSymlinkCommand: true,        // optional\n  trustedDirs: [\"/opt/homebrew\"],   // optional\n  timeoutMs: 5000,                   // optional\n  maxOutputBytes: 1048576            // optional\n}\n```\n\n## 1Password/op Provider Configuration\n\nThe documented example shows:\n\n```json5\n{\n  source: \"exec\",\n  command: \"/opt/homebrew/bin/op\",\n  allowSymlinkCommand: true,\n  trustedDirs: [\"/opt/homebrew\"],\n  args: [\"read\", \"op://Personal/OpenClaw QA API Key/password\"],\n  passEnv: [\"HOME\"],\n  jsonOnly: false\n}\n```\n\n## Binding to Model Providers\n\nA model provider's apiKey references a secret using the SecretRef object contract:\n\n```json5\n{\n  source: \"exec\",\n  provider: \"onepassword_openai\",\n  id: \"value\"\n}\n```\n\nThe `provider` field names the configured secrets provider; the `id` specifies what to retrieve from it.\n\n## Steps to Add a New Provider Secret\n\n1. \"Audit current state\" with `openclaw secrets audit --check`\n2. \"Configure and apply SecretRefs\" using `openclaw secrets configure --apply`\n3. \"Re-audit\" to verify the migration is complete","durationMs":5962,"url":"https://docs.openclaw.ai/gateway/secrets"},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"6624ba5a-25fc-4f69-b62d-f8b73e54b312","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/logan","sessionId":"4f03d270-3e64-41cc-b325-30871ab76d55","version":"2.1.202","gitBranch":"HEA