{"parentUuid":"7880fb98-6093-4391-b296-c85228d2da31","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"482ddd9f-82c5-483b-a812-503c9a24889c","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01D73mqBEE1pKRtQRdyhyrpR","type":"tool_result","content":"# Android Chat Message Flow to Gateway\n\n## Message Transmission\n\nWhen a user types in the Chat tab, the Android app sends the message via the `chat.send` RPC method to the gateway, which then triggers an agent run on the session.\n\n## Required Device Token Roles and Scopes\n\nThe device token requires the **`node` role** (not operator). Based on the documentation, the token needs the `chat.send` scope to transmit messages. The exact phrasing indicates: \"Send: `chat.send`\"\n\n## Conditions for No Agent Reply\n\nA message could append to the session transcript but produce **no agent run** when:\n- The gateway receives the `chat.send` call but the agent execution fails silently\n- Offline queuing occurs (messages are cached locally but not yet delivered to the gateway)\n- The session is disconnected or the node loses gateway connectivity\n\nThe docs note that Android maintains \"queued offline messages are delivered only to the gateway they were written for,\" implying messages can persist without immediate execution.\n\n## chat.subscribe vs chat.send\n\n- **`chat.send`**: The RPC method that transmits user messages to the gateway and triggers agent processing\n- **`chat.subscribe`**: Receives \"push updates (best-effort)\" from the gateway back to the Android client, subscribing to `event:\"chat\"` for real-time message delivery and session updates"}]},"uuid":"67a9c61e-7ffa-48fd-bbf3-fd62eb070f95","timestamp":"2026-07-07T05:48:40.881Z","toolUseResult":{"bytes":19652,"code":200,"codeText":"OK","result":"# Android Chat Message Flow to Gateway\n\n## Message Transmission\n\nWhen a user types in the Chat tab, the Android app sends the message via the `chat.send` RPC method to the gateway, which then triggers an agent run on the session.\n\n## Required Device Token Roles and Scopes\n\nThe device token requires the **`node` role** (not operator). Based on the documentation, the token needs the `chat.send` scope to transmit messages. The exact phrasing indicates: \"Send: `chat.send`\"\n\n## Conditions for No Agent Reply\n\nA message could append to the session transcript but produce **no agent run** when:\n- The gateway receives the `chat.send` call but the agent execution fails silently\n- Offline queuing occurs (messages are cached locally but not yet delivered to the gateway)\n- The session is disconnected or the node loses gateway connectivity\n\nThe docs note that Android maintains \"queued offline messages are delivered only to the gateway they were written for,\" implying messages can persist without immediate execution.\n\n## chat.subscribe vs chat.send\n\n- **`chat.send`**: The RPC method that transmits user messages to the gateway and triggers agent processing\n- **`chat.subscribe`**: Receives \"push updates (best-effort)\" from the gateway back to the Android client, subscribing to `event:\"chat\"` for real-time message delivery and session updates","durationMs":4704,"url":"https://docs.openclaw.ai/platforms/android"},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"7880fb98-6093-4391-b296-c85228d2da31","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/logan","sessionId":"4f03d270-3e64-41cc-b325-30871ab76d55","version":"2.1.202","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"your-18-entry-list-is-cached-gadget"}
