pairing` (Pixel device token has `operator.approvals/read/talk.secrets/write`); present since at least 07-03, unrelated to the failure.\n\n## Leading theory — version skew\n\nLogan attests phone chat **worked ~2026-07-03** once the gateway first stabilized (the gateway log's only `chat.send` ever, 07-03 19:03 with an image attachment, is plausibly it). The app is very new and iterating daily **in-tree**: mobile-chat substrate (reconnect resume cursors openclaw/openclaw#100197, offline session cache openclaw/openclaw#100194, streaming replay openclaw/openclaw#100196) all landed **07-05/06**; three `fix(android)` PRs merged 07-07 alone (incl. reconnect fix openclaw/openclaw#101519). Installed gateway `2026.6.11` (Jun 30) is the latest **stable**; the app tracks the `2026.7.1-beta` / main line. An app auto-update in the 07-03→07-06 gap whose new offline-cache send shape files-without-dispatching on the older stable gateway fits every observation.\n\n## Thaw options (suspended state — see `CLAUDE-SESSION-2026-07-06.md` § Suspension)\n\n- **A (cheapest):** update the Android app on the phone, resend, watch the log.\n- **B:** move the gateway to `2026.7.1-beta.2` to match the app's era. ⚠️ `openclaw update` wipes the Obsidian origin patch — re-run `~/.openclaw/patch-obsidian-origin.sh` immediately after (config survives).\n- **C:** file upstream at openclaw/openclaw with this repro + both version numbers (needs app version from the phone). External contact gated on Logan.\n\nForensic note for whoever picks this up: the authoritative gateway log is `~/Library/Logs/openclaw/gateway.log`; `/tmp/openclaw/openclaw-<local-date>.log` is CLI/child-process noise. A working send's log signature is `[tool-policy]` + `[model-fetch]` within seconds — inbound send methods are **not** logged at INFO, so absence of `chat.send` lines proves nothing.\n\n---\n*Filed by Claude Code at Logan's direction (\"UPDATE GitHub surface\"), mirroring session task #27. Transparent AI authorship.*\n\n`C