{"parentUuid":"cf796166-a029-48d6-b611-5196eafa7f38","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_011CcqmDoFCGyDtDGg9z989P","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01VDhSmdKMBtyTeBvexQpfHh","name":"ExitPlanMode","input":{"allowedPrompts":[{"tool":"Bash","prompt":"read-only git and openclaw/hermes config-get checks to confirm the flat chains are unchanged"}],"plan":"# Simplify one, for real — BEEFSTACK *is* the flat fallback list\n\n## Context\n\nThe lesson Logan drew tonight from a five-second question I turned into an hours-long ordeal: agents build machinery that **reads** as rigor and thereby dodges the \"is this actually right?\" check a simple thing would fail instantly. \"Code that defies logic\" = built to look right instead of be right. Chosen target to fix, for real: **BEEFSTACK.**\n\nBEEFSTACK's actual thesis is one sentence — *redundancy: diversify model routing by provider **bucket** so one provider dying doesn't kill a run* (\"belts and suspenders and a third thing\"). That thesis is **already fully met by a flat, bucket-diverse fallback list in config.** Tonight the flat list proved it in production: OpenClaw's chain fell past the drained OpenRouter pool to the Direct-Mistral BYOK rung (`api.mistral.ai`, HTTP 200, 1.6 s) and answered Logan's real message.\n\nThe *elaborate* BEEFSTACK — issue #690's \"Viable Systems Loop\" capability router (Router Core → Capability Analyzer → Tier Resolver → Provider Selector → Locality Resolver → Cost Manager → Hygiene Filter → Endpoint: **8 components + 6 open design decisions**) — has read \"implementation: not started\" since 2026-06-29 (40+ days) and has shipped **zero** redundancy the flat list doesn't already provide. No code was ever written. The machinery is the *design, the issue, the task, and the \"not the real thing yet\" framing* — that is what gets removed.\n\n## Recommended approach — remove machinery, add nothing\n\nThe flat, bucket-diverse fallback chain already live in two config files **is** BEEFSTACK. Everything above it is retired, not built.\n\n1. **Canonize the flat chain as the system.** In `BEEFSTACK-MODEL-ROUTING-2026-05-17.md`, state plainly that the live fallback chains are BEEFSTACK — not a \"static fallback projection\" or a down-payment on a future router. The one non-trivial rule the thesis needs — *don't retry the same exhausted provider bucket* — is already expressed as **BYOK-aware ordering within the list.** Ordering a list does not require a Cost Manager or a Tier Resolver.\n   - Config files stay exactly as they run (do not touch behavior): `~/.hermes/config.yaml` (`fallback_providers`), `~/.openclaw/openclaw.json` (`agents.defaults.model`).\n2. **Retire the router design.** Rescope/close #690 from \"design + build the 8-component router\" to \"the flat bucket-diverse chain is the routing system.\" Dissolve the 6 open design decisions — they gate a thing that isn't needed. Cite tonight's production save as the evidence.\n3. **Retire task #22** — mark superseded by the working flat chain; any residual repoints to routine \"maintain the fallback chains,\" not a build.\n4. **Drop the L4 aspiration** wherever the stack is framed (this plan file's own old L0–L4 diagram included) — BEEFSTACK is not a pending top-of-stack build; it is config that already runs.\n\n**Honest boundary (the one thing the router does that the list doesn't):** *capability-aware* routing — sending a coding task to a coding model, a reasoning task to a reasoner. That is a separate, speculative axis from redundancy, and the flat list does not do it. The simplification is not \"capability routing is worthless\" — it is: **don't build an 8-component VSM to get it.** If it's ever genuinely wanted, it is a small per-request model hint, added then, on evidence of need — not a pipeline standing gated for months. The redundancy job, the one with production proof, is *done.*\n\n## What this deliberately does NOT do\n\n- Build a router, classifier, or any component.\n- Add or change any live config or daemon behavior.\n- Delete code (there is none) — this shrinks doctrine/issue/task footprint only.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `openclaw config get agents.defaults.model` + `~/.hermes/config.yaml` `fallback_providers` unchanged — the working chains keep running.\n- One test send per daemon still returns a reply through the chain (as tonight: `OPENCLAW_RESPONDS_OK` via the Mistral rung; `HERMES_RESPONDS_OK`).\n- #690 reads rescoped/closed with the flat chain canonical; task #22 retired; `BEEFSTACK-MODEL-ROUTING-2026-05-17.md` states the flat chain is the system, not a placeholder.\n- Net: doctrine/issue/task footprint *shrinks*; zero new code, zero new config.\n","planFilePath":"/Users/logan/.claude/plans/your-18-entry-list-is-cached-gadget.md"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1818,"cache_read_input_tokens":915789,"output_tokens":109,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1818,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":109,"cache_read_input_tokens":915789,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1818,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1818},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CcqmDiEa8BALW6LMZhbbs","type":"assistant","uuid":"9e284d2f-9212-4a1c-8de3-a66329b34fa1","timestamp":"2026-07-09T03:20:33.869Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-4-8","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/logan","sessionId":"4f03d270-3e64-41cc-b325-30871ab76d55","version":"2.1.202","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"your-18-entry-list-is-cached-gadget"}
