{"parentUuid":"0e0660e5-48fa-4d0f-acf1-a3a1b38374e3","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"873b5f4d-88f5-45d1-a8fd-93dbea74b293","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_014tFiuDScGRjcaAncK8RoWf","type":"tool_result","content":"# \"The Party's Over, Isla de Señorita\" Episode Summary\n\n**Plot Overview:**\nThe episode focuses on Ice King's obsession with Princess Bubblegum reaching a breaking point. After his fixation on capturing her causes problems, Ice King ends up on Isla de Señorita, a living island, where he encounters the Island Lady.\n\n**Key Events:**\nIce King's behavior toward princesses—particularly his creepy obsession with Bubblegum—finally has serious consequences. On the island, he meets the Island Lady and forms an unlikely friendship. Party God arrives as a romantic interest for the Island Lady, but behaves disrespectfully toward her. Ice King intervenes, fighting Party God in an aerial battle to defend her honor.\n\n**The Conflict & Resolution:**\nIce King uses Party God as a puppet so the Island Lady can express her frustrations. Through this interaction, Ice King experiences genuine emotional growth and even provides surprisingly accurate psychological analysis of Princess Bubblegum, showing that \"parts of Simon do shine into his subconscious.\" The episode ends with Ice King promising to change, though his closing line—\"ah, we'll work it out\"—suggests his improvements are temporary.\n\n**Themes:**\nThe review emphasizes that friendship and emotional support are crucial to Ice King's mental health. While the crown prevents lasting change, the episode demonstrates his capacity for maturity and sanity when given caring companionship, offering hope that \"a friend can go a long way for the sad iceman.\""}]},"uuid":"1f716ed9-c0ce-4595-b6d7-a4d271683c3a","timestamp":"2026-07-09T03:34:50.428Z","toolUseResult":{"bytes":155021,"code":200,"codeText":"OK","result":"# \"The Party's Over, Isla de Señorita\" Episode Summary\n\n**Plot Overview:**\nThe episode focuses on Ice King's obsession with Princess Bubblegum reaching a breaking point. After his fixation on capturing her causes problems, Ice King ends up on Isla de Señorita, a living island, where he encounters the Island Lady.\n\n**Key Events:**\nIce King's behavior toward princesses—particularly his creepy obsession with Bubblegum—finally has serious consequences. On the island, he meets the Island Lady and forms an unlikely friendship. Party God arrives as a romantic interest for the Island Lady, but behaves disrespectfully toward her. Ice King intervenes, fighting Party God in an aerial battle to defend her honor.\n\n**The Conflict & Resolution:**\nIce King uses Party God as a puppet so the Island Lady can express her frustrations. Through this interaction, Ice King experiences genuine emotional growth and even provides surprisingly accurate psychological analysis of Princess Bubblegum, showing that \"parts of Simon do shine into his subconscious.\" The episode ends with Ice King promising to change, though his closing line—\"ah, we'll work it out\"—suggests his improvements are temporary.\n\n**Themes:**\nThe review emphasizes that friendship and emotional support are crucial to Ice King's mental health. While the crown prevents lasting change, the episode demonstrates his capacity for maturity and sanity when given caring companionship, offering hope that \"a friend can go a long way for the sad iceman.\"","durationMs":5544,"url":"https://adventuretimereviewed.com/2018/01/02/the-partys-over-isla-de-senorita-review/"},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"0e0660e5-48fa-4d0f-acf1-a3a1b38374e3","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/logan","sessionId":"4f03d270-3e64-41cc-b325-30871ab76d55","version":"2.1.202","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"your-18-entry-list-is-cached-gadget"}
